==== 2026-09-05T07:08Z repo=29b9742 comparison=lithium ====
# matt-42/lithium, single_headers @ 2026-09-05, one thread (s::nthreads = 1,
# s::ip = "127.0.0.1"), route "/" answering "OK". Same box, same htgen, same
# minute as the two webmachine lines above.
#
# Two corrections were needed to run it here, neither of them about speed:
# without s::ip it binds AF_INET6 and this host has no IPv6, and the s::ip
# path binds `addr.sin_port = port` with no htons - an upstream bug, fixed
# in the local checkout only.
#
# The two servers do not answer the same bytes: lithium 94 per response
# (92 head + 2 body), webmachine 155 (116 head + 39 body).
harness: /home/user/asmod4n/htgen/htgen -c64 -d10s h1 (one ring, one thread) transport=tcp
lithium:    rps=157592 / 147845   server=99.7% of one core   MB/s=14.13 / 13.25
webmachine: rps=219666 / 193397   server=98% of one core     MB/s=32.47 / 28.59
# Both are server-bound, so the numbers measure the servers. At -c192 on
# this 4-vCPU container the order turns: lithium 153104, webmachine 140192.
