# litespeedtech/openlitespeed, built from git today (the mod_security
# target does not link here - no YAJL - so only the openlitespeed target
# was built; the module has no part in this arm). Same box, same htgen,
# same minute as the two webmachine lines below.
#
# WHAT OPENLITESPEED GETS, its best foot on this box: httpdWorkers 1
# (apples to our one thread), logLevel ERROR, access log to /dev/null,
# gzip off, keepalive 10000 requests, eventDispatcher epoll, and the
# cache module OFF. The last two are not cosmetic: with the shipped
# "best" dispatcher and ls_enabled 1 the same run answers 30k instead
# of 40k, and the cache module sits in front of every request.
#
# The two servers do not answer the same bytes: openlitespeed 244 per
# response (a static file with ETag, Last-Modified and Accept-Ranges),
